{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504057-essence-do-dragon-blooded-always-kill-their-steed","id":1504057,"title":"[Essence] Do Dragon-Blooded always kill their steed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T10:24:10-08:00","id":1504057,"title":"[Essence] Do Dragon-Blooded always kill their steed?","content":"So the wording of the Dragon-Blooded Anima specifies that it affects &quot;any non-DB in close range&quot;. Does that mean a Dragon-Blooded has to dismount themselves after spending 5 motes or risk killing their steed? I haven't seen a charm that negates such effect, nor any mention of any protection being offered to a Prince's loyal mount so I got curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T12:56:23-08:00","id":1504068,"title":"","content":"Traditionally, yes?<br /> <br /> It's one level of damage a round.<br /> <br /> You could easily make a custom charm/mode/artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T16:13:54-08:00","id":1504083,"title":"","content":"This is also an issue in 3e as well. Homebrewing in a Charm or Mode or whatever to protect your mount seems like the most reasonable option.<br /> <br /> Aside from using a chariot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T20:39:34-08:00","id":1504099,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a problem and I recall that it was noted in one of the First or Second edition books as the reason why the Realm traditionally did not tend to employ mounted horsemen as a major part of their military tactics. That said I'm pretty sure there was a Ride charm that allowed a Dragon Blooded to avoid killing their mount, which would pretty much be mandatory for any Dragon Blooded planning to use Ride charms. Don't know if it's in 3rd edition. If it's not, add it because otherwise it'll be problematic for any Dragon Blooded that decides to heavily invest in the Ride charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T22:27:09-08:00","id":1504105,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall 2e also having an artifact saddle that nullfied Anima Flux caused by the rider. Which would be another reason not to field Exalted cavalry units; too expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T00:15:46-08:00","id":1504109,"title":"","content":"There's a Ride 3 Essence 3 Charm (Elemental Halo's Mercy) in 2E that prevents a mount from taking anima flux damage for a scene. The same Charm was Ride 4, Essence 3 in 1E, though it was in a late release Aspect Book. Sounds like that doesn't exist in 3E/Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-01-2023, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T01:51:55-08:00","id":1504110,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Among-Horses Exaltation is a Ride 5/Essence 3 DB 3e Charm. It's also the Wood Signature Charm for Ride. You can only use it on one mount, but that mount increases its natural Hardness (even from zero) by 1, meaning it's immune to Anima Flux from both the rider and their companions; as well as other boosts. It's also a permanent enhancement Charm to your mount, not something you have to activate every unit of time. So any DB that's going to ride into battle is probably going to pick this up and use it on their favored mount.<br /> <br /> Edit: Essence also as Rider-and-Mount Unity, with a DB mode Great Heart Companion in Navigate that protects your current mount from anima damage.<br /> <br /> So, no need to house rule anything, it's already in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 03-01-2023, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T05:45:07-08:00","id":1504115,"title":"","content":"Additionally, in Ex3 combat most mounts share an initiative track with the rider and cannot be targeted by withering attacks. The only way Anima Flux can touch them during combat is if you rule they count as trivial opponents... which is a take. Obviously the 1L a minute outside of combat isn't great for your loyal steed but normally way less of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T06:16:26-08:00","id":1504117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504057-essence-do-dragon-blooded-always-kill-their-steed?p=1504110#post1504110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Among-Horses Exaltation is a Ride 5/Essence 3 DB 3e Charm. It's also the Wood Signature Charm for Ride. You can only use it on one mount, but that mount increases its natural Hardness (even from zero) by 1, meaning it's immune to Anima Flux from both the rider and their companions; as well as other boosts. It's also a permanent enhancement Charm to your mount, not something you have to activate every unit of time. So any DB that's going to ride into battle is probably going to pick this up and use it on their favored mount.<br /> <br /> Edit: Essence also as Rider-and-Mount Unity, with a DB mode Great Heart Companion in Navigate that protects your current mount from anima damage.<br /> <br /> So, no need to house rule anything, it's already in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh it was a mode of a universal charm, that's why I missed it.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T05:53:17-08:00","id":1504255,"title":"","content":"There are ride charms and a special artifact saddle from 2nd edition that protect the animal from that anima damage, it's a feature not a flaw, and why most dragon blooded prefer to fight on foot and are also a danger to thier troops as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}